d only ```"],["5f6fb9dc_b5127190",4,0,1,"```suggestion UserSiteAccess::kOnClick. However, for some reason it seems the toggle ```"]],0,935],[7108403,20396,99,2.361,1.866,[[0,555]],[],0,936],[7122872,20397,57,1.341,1.058,[[0,556]],[],0,937],[7123298,20397,80,2.361,1.866,[[0,557]],[],0,938],[7125303,20398,58,1.341,1.058,[[0,558]],[],0,939],[7124904,20398,12,0.421,0.3,[[0,559]],[],0,940],[7124353,20398,4,0.259,0.185,[[2,265]],[],0,941],[7125804,20399,4,0.259,0.185,[[2,266]],[],0,942],[7126990,20400,20,0.737,0.556,[[0,560]],[["f196255b_a6819089",4,-1,0,"nit: long time ago"]],0,943],[6986392,20403,308,7.601,6.192,[[0,561]],[["",29,-27,0]],0,944],[7138129,20404,60,1.341,1.058,[[0,562]],[["077ffac3_2d0f2d93",4,0,1,"```suggestion the existent crash keys). This is weird because if the toggle is ```"],["20d9484c_94edeb3e",28,0,1,"We're passing in the web contents, but we're setting the URL as the value, so I think we could swap \"web contents\" for \"URL\" here and below to be more accurate?"],["24472d6e_745f8315",28,0,1,"```suggestion // The current URL (hostname) when GrantSiteAccess() was called. ```"],["4034e383_5f09273a",4,0,1,"Here and below to be consistent with the above. ```suggestion site access is UserSiteAccess::kOnAllSites. This is weird because if toggle is ```"],["5976e564_3c13a9f4",4,0,1,"I think this could be removed, the rest of the message describes is pretty well."],["5ddec18c_b3b5cbc9",28,0,1,"`GURL::spec()` can assert if the GURL is not valid, but if it's valid then I think .spec() should not assert. So I think to avoid a crash here it could be: ```suggestion if (!web_contents) { return…"],["8ad43574_13360138",4,0,1,"```suggestion [Extensions] Additional crash keys when granting site access via menu ```"],["8c284e01_e07fe932",28,0,1,"```suggestion // TODO(crbug.com/456129773): Remove crash keys when site toggle crash is fixed. ```"],["96fff6e7_a318cd3e",4,0,1,"```suggestion computation. This will help us narrow down which computation is the cause. ```"],